    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced, arguing against committing to either extreme. The bull case rests on strong but stale fundamentals ($39.9B quarterly operating cash flow, $30.6B returned to shareholders, $353.5B total assets) from December 30, 2023 \u2014 nearly four months stale. The bear case rests on current, live technical data that is uniformly bearish: price below all major moving averages, fresh MACD bearish crossover, RSI at 37.90 trending down, and accelerating downside momentum (5-day return of -6.54% nearly double the 20-day return of -3.72%). However, the bear has produced zero evidence of fundamental deterioration, and a 15% drawdown on a company generating $40B in quarterly operating cash flow with aggressive buybacks does not warrant exiting entirely. The risk/reward is roughly symmetric (~5% downside to $155 vs ~6% upside to the declining 50 SMA), so maintaining current exposure at ~$163.22 without adding or exiting is the prudent stance. I will wait for a confirmed reversal signal \u2014 a daily close above the 10 EMA ($167.36) or better the 50 SMA ($173.24) \u2014 before adding, and trim 25-50% if price breaks below $162.31 and then $160.\n\n**Entry Price**: 167.36\n\n**Stop Loss**: 160.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/benchmark weight, no more than 5% of portfolio. No leverage until a confirmed reversal.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
